Street-Fighting Mathematics — Mahajan (@ql-source-street: 0, is #book, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_082F9E0A0TMB43HS5DHW4PZHSA
Sanjoy Mahajan. Street-Fighting Mathematics: The Art of Educated Guessing and Opportunistic Problem Solving. MIT Press, 2010. Foreword by Carver A. Mead. English. ISBN 978-0-262-51429-3.

[MIT OCW reading guide](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-098-street-fighting-mathematics-january-iap-2008/pages/readings/) · [Authorized complete PDF](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-098-street-fighting-mathematics-january-iap-2008/mit18_098iap08_draft_text.pdf).

Use the actual PDF's contents when assigning pages: the retrieved complete file contains the published 2010 edition, although its URL and some surrounding OCW descriptions still say draft. Its chapters are Dimensions, Easy cases, Lumping, Pictorial proofs, Taking out the big part, and Analogy. The older chapter-by-chapter OCW reading table uses different headings and pagination. Chapter names, not that table's page numbers, identify the reading here.

The PDF's publication notice states CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 United States and credits Mahajan, Mead, and MIT Press. Preserve that notice and component credits. Its derivations become demanding; use the trail's algebra and geometric preparation and return to unfamiliar calculus through the appropriate mathematical reading. The complete book is an advanced continuation, not an arithmetic prerequisite. Contents and edition notice checked on 28 October 2026. No PDF is bundled.

**Return:** [Quantitative literacy sources — books, standards, and articles](../Sources.lingua#r_7MMXWNA1B4YGA271KMHPPJEK9Q).
